  "worked_solution": "The third equation states that ${x}_{3}=-\\frac{1}{3}.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}-6(-\\frac{1}{3})=3\\,\u27f9\\,{x}_{2}=3-2=1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{3}=-\\frac{1}{3}$ and ${x}_{2}=1$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+1-(-\\frac{1}{3})=2\\,\u27f9\\,{x}_{1}=2-1-\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=\\frac{2}{3}$, ${x}_{2}=1$, and ${x}_{3}=-\\frac{1}{3}.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as\n$[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}].$",
